  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Mon Apr 20 2026\n\nSome lingering light showers are possible over extreme southeast \nportions of the forecast area (northwest Hill Country) Tuesday \nnight into Wednesday morning, otherwise mainly a dry forecast for \nthe remainder of the work week. The next upper level trough will\ntrack across the northern Rockies and into the upper Midwest by \nmid to late week. At this time, it appears that any precipitation\nassociated with this system will remain north and east of the \narea. Warmer temperatures are expected beginning Wednesday and \ncontinuing through next weekend. Highs on Wednesday closer to \nnormal for this time of year, with highs in the upper 70s and \nlower 80s. Temperatures will then warm into the 80s Thursday \nthrough the following Monday, with overnight lows mainly in the \n60s. \n\nLooks like southwest flow aloft by late next weekend, as models \nshow a shortwave developing over the southwest CONUS. While this \nsystem could result in a chance for sowers and thunderstorms by \nthis time, model confidence remains low and current NBM 20 POPs \nseem reasonable for now.",
